        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/7.1.1/E5_Event"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/7.1.1/Place"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property relates an Event to a spatial anchor—physical or digital—used to situate the event in space when such contextualization is meaningful. It is intentionally broad and optional: many events can be spatially located in principle, but the location may be unknown, irrelevant, or not recorded. Use hasSpatialLocus for lightweight contextual placement (e.g., an interaction occurring in a messaging platform, an assignment made within an institutional system, a reaction recorded via a device), without implying that the event has a formal venue or that spatial information is a primary descriptive feature.

Typical use: contextual, “if needed” spatialization of any event (including non-programmed or non-operational events).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


